// A reference model is reachable four ways — `all()`, `getById`, `getByName`,
// `getBySlug` — and the last three read `BaseModel`'s lazily-built index rather
// than calling `all()`. Patching one accessor replaces ONE route to the rows:
// production code that reaches them another way gets the real dataset while the
// test asserts on fixtures, and the failure reads as a component bug. Turning
// the crawler lookups into the indexed resolver broke 17 tests in five suites
// at once, every one of which had patched `all` alone. `patchModelRows`
// (test/patchModel.ts) patches every accessor.
//
// Matches the accessor on `SalvageUnionReference.<Model>` directly; binding the
// model to a local first evades it.
language js(typescript, jsx)

JsAssignmentExpression(left=$target) as $assign where {
  $target <: r"^SalvageUnionReference\.\w+\.(?:all|getById|getByName|getBySlug|find|findAll)$",
  register_diagnostic(span=$assign, message="Patch reference-model rows with patchModelRows(model, rows) from test/patchModel.ts, which covers every accessor.", severity="error")
}
